Part 4 — Select the AI/ML Approach — 10 Points

Answer the following.

Would you use supervised or unsupervised learning?
Choose:

X Supervised Learning
☐ Unsupervised Learning
☐ Not sure

Explain your choice.
The model can learn from historical data of demand and sales. It can use the information given to it to predict future values for these based on recent numbers.
Write 4-6 sentences.

Would the problem involve classification or prediction?
Choose:

☐ Classification
x Prediction
☐ Both
☐ Neither

Explain your choice.
The model would be using previous data to predict future values. these future values would be used for ordering and stocking rules
Write 4-6 sentences.

Part 5 — Data Quality and Business Impact — 10 Points

Identify three possible data-quality problems.
Missing data, Incorrect Inventory, Outdated information are the the most impactful
Examples:

Missing information
Incorrect values
Duplicate records
Outdated information
Inconsistent formats
Biased data
What could happen if the data is poor?
Poor data can give inaccurate predictions. These predictions are what the company bases their choices off, so if the predictions are wrong, the company will make poor decisions.
Consider:

Poor data → Poor model → Poor business decision

Part 6 — Complete AI Solution Summary

Complete this final section:

Business Problem - Determine how much inventory to order.

Data Needed - Sales, inventory, lead times, seasonal demand, industry trends

Features and Target - Historical sales, current inventory, Lead time, Seasonality, Stockout history

AI/ML Approach - Use historical data to predict future values

Data Quality - Missing data, Incorrect Inventory, Outdated information

Type of Learning - Supervised

Model Output - Predict future demand

Business Benefit - Reduce excess, minimize stockouts, lower inventory costs

Potential Risk - Poor data can give inaccurate predictions



Assignment Example

Here is an example

Business Problem

A telecommunications company wants to identify customers who are likely to cancel their subscriptions.

Data Needed

The company could use:

Customer tenure
Monthly bill
Number of complaints
Internet usage
Contract type
Number of support calls
Learning Type

Supervised learning

Why?

Because the company has historical data showing which customers previously cancelled.

Classification or Prediction?

Classification

The model could classify customers as:

Likely to Churn / Not Likely to Churn

Data Quality Problems

The company might have:

Missing customer information
Incorrect billing information
Duplicate customer records
Business Benefit

The company could identify high-risk customers and offer them discounts or improved services before they leave.

Potential Risk

The model could incorrectly identify customers as high-risk, resulting in unnecessary discounts or marketing expenses.

